    },
    {
      "entry": 15262,
      "name": "Obsidian Eradicator",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:15262:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:a5be95471eb06dc20590c3e1",
            "source:4d69deed0a83557974459bb5",
            "source:c31fe11974e6dd900a6a304c"
          ],
          "text": "An Obsidian Eradicator can drop an Ancient Qiraji Artifact. The artifact begins Secrets of the Qiraji, whose instructions direct its holder to dragons near the temple entrance.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 15262
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 15263,
      "name": "The Prophet Skeram",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:15263:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:47efb47ee2e7ec36a6d3b885",
            "source:16e86e1df55215cb299c236b",
            "source:8087518ad2ace5746c3ab80c",
            "source:c73c79ff9c0d47dec9c7526f",
            "source:7e2031152604ade7a061e99f",
            "source:58e3711048330550df41fdca"
          ],
          "text": "The Prophet Skeram taunts mortals and threatens death, while warning that an age of darkness is at hand. He calls for the return of the ancient ones, a cause he presents as imminent.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 15263
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 15264,
      "name": "Anubisath Sentinel",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:15264:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:f29bc2fabd272431fd53580c",
            "source:6893d9084bbee99159dd72f6",
            "source:14196725a051bb80a325843b"
          ],
          "text": "Anubisath Sentinel is an Ahn'Qiraj sentinel that shares its powers with its brethren and can become enraged in battle.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 15264
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 15275,
      "name": "Emperor Vek'nilash",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:15275:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:5288bc164f8ce6b57020c6e8",
            "source:8f366e37022a95373b281a0a",
            "source:d3727c5342fadb746304db22",
            "source:f86236985978290fed0251cf",
            "source:9f94cd7f8fce3c7f421d5abf"
          ],
          "text": "Emperor Vek'nilash welcomes intruders alongside his brother Vek'lor and speaks of shared pain. His concern for Vek'lor is explicit when he cries out to him at his own death; otherwise, he taunts and threatens those who enter the emperors' lair.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 15275
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 15276,
      "name": "Emperor Vek'lor",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:15276:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:144e759469e5fd69450aa56d",
            "source:3c2d79259d4ade32ae75cf77",
            "source:061aad81825bdb4b4c85992b",
            "source:680f2d8cbb93c94ac948d6bd",
            "source:06658cbf066999fe66ed5916"
          ],
          "text": "Emperor Vek'lor regards mortals as easy prey and threatens them with pain and death. His cry of ‘My brother, no!’ reveals a personal bond beneath his hostility toward intruders.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 15276
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 15277,
      "name": "Anubisath Defender",
